iles listing, project_context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source_code, requirement_states), context (task ID 5301), execution_constitution, go_style_constitution, task description, constraints, shared_protocols, and package_contracts.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/md5sum/main.go` implementing R1.1-R1.4 using pkg/hashutil\n   - Create `cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go` with differential tests against gmd5sum\n   - Run `go build -o bin/md5sum ./cmd/md5sum/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/md5sum/` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/md5sum/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file at `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd030-md5sum.yaml` and was about to begin implementation. I had gathered all necessary context:\n   - R1.1: GNU format output (\"HASH  FILENAME\" or \"HASH *FILENAME\")\n   - R1.2: Stdin reading with \"-\" filename\n   - R1.3: --tag BSD format \"MD5 (FILENAME) = HASH\"\n   - R1.4: Exit 1 on file errors, continue processing\n   - Design: crypto/md5.New, DigestLen 16, DigestFiles for core workflow, InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n   \n   No code has been written yet. The implementation plan is:\n   - main.go: flag parsing (--binary/-b, --text/-t, --tag, --check/-c, --warn/-w, --quiet, --status), HashConfig with Algorithm=\"MD5\", NewHash=md5.New, DigestLen=16, branch on --check vs digest mode, call DigestFiles or VerifyChecksums\n   - For R1.1-R1.4 scope: need at minimum -b, --tag flags and file args, delegating to hashutil.DigestFiles\n   - md5sum_test.go: TestDiff using BuildBinary, exec.LookPath(\"gmd5sum\"), RunDiffTests with test cases for stdin, file, --tag, missing file\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/md5sum/main.go` and `cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go` following the write-all-then-build strategy from the go_style_constitution. The main.go should:\n   - Start with SPDX copyright header\n   - Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n   - Parse flags